                <head>ETA–22. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On March 24, 1959, Acting Secretary Dillon approved a recommendation contained in a memorandum from
                        Wilson T. M. Beale, Jr., Deputy
                    Assistant Secretary of State for Economic Affairs (initialled by Assistant
                    Secretary Mann), to authorize Assistant Secretary of the Treasury Upton to sign the Final Act incorporating the
                    articles of agreement for an Inter-American Economic Development Banking
                    Institution prepared by the Socialized Committee of the Organization of American
                    States. The memorandum reads in part as follows: “Initialling the Final Act of
                    the Specialized Committee will constitute in effect a commitment on the part of
                    the United States not to propose any alteration in the draft charter since we
                    have so proposed to the other countries. Subsequent signing of the Final Act
                    will signify in effect United States agreement to accept or reject the draft
                    charter in toto, without reservations, after customary legislative action.”
                    (810.10/1–559)</p>
            </div>
